      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'm going to remake the gallery to remove the 2 missing images, but these were the steps I usually take when updating that specific gallery (which is multiple times a week, sometimes multiple times in a day):\n\n1. I click on post an image in the group gallery and upload a new version of the image I want to replace (for context, these are speedrun and time trial leaderboards).\n\n2. I add the new image to the group gallery\n\n3. I delete the old version of the image from the group gallery\n\n4. I go to my personal gallery and delete the old image permanently\n\nSo I'm assuming something went wrong on step 3 or 4 where the group gallery version didn't actually get removed and since the image doesn't exist its stuck as an hourglass image and lacking the delete options.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
